          },
          {
            "end": 6224,
            "start": 5927,
            "type": "TextPositionSelector"
          },
          {
            "exact": "And the more should it be so that the method of solving the land problem has been elaborated by Henry George to such a degree of perfection that, under the existing State organization and compulsory taxation it is impossible to invent any other better, more just, practical, and peaceful solution.",
            "prefix": "",
            "suffix": "",
            "type": "TextQuoteSelector"
          },
          {
            "type": "ProgressionSelector",
            "value": 0.7323544839912962
          },
